    {
      "id": "4f90abd8362c53850ef7c3476c237f5c0d9f61a9",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 404412295,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi,\nIn my opinion this is a fault in the application and i doubt very much many application encode the messages in this way. From the trace you sent privatly:\n:\nopCode: globalValue (1)\n00.. .... = Class: UNIVERSAL (0)\n..0. .... = P/C: Primitive Encoding\n...0 0110 = Tag: OBJECT IDENTIFIER (6)\nLength: 1\nglobalValue: 1.5 (iso.5)\n\nUsing the tag 6 for what should be a local value is plain wrong...or using a numerical walue for an OID.\n\nFrom a working application:\nopCode: localValue (0)\n00.. .... = Class: UNIVERSAL (0)\n..0. .... = P/C: Primitive Encoding\n...0 0010 = Tag: INTEGER (2)\nLength: 1\nlocalValue: sendRoutingInfo (22)\n\nSo either put a proper OID as the global value or encode as local value...\n\nBest regards\nAnders",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-08-31T06:51:54.536Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-08-31T06:51:54.536Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 68925296,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
